+# Leave Mystic Enchants out of scroll rolls when the server does not have their spell (they would
+# apply and do nothing). Checked at every startup, not a fixed list: an enchant whose spell is added
+# later (Spell.dbc or spell_dbc) rolls again after the next restart. Owned and collected enchants are
+# not touched. 0 = roll every enchant, as before.
+CoA.MysticEnchants.SkipMissingSpells = 1
+
+# Also leave out enchants whose spell exists but does nothing on this server: only placeholder effects
+# (dummy or script effects, or a trigger aura with nothing to trigger) and no spell script,
+# spell_linked_spell, coa_mystic_enchant_proc or coa_mystic_enchant_aura_link row giving it behaviour.
+# Checked at every startup, not a fixed list: an enchant rolls again once it is given behaviour. Known
+# limit: enchants that work only through hard-coded checks in C++ look the same and are left out too.
+# 0 = roll them anyway.
+CoA.MysticEnchants.SkipDudSpells = 1
+
